<title>ITALY: Italian refinery runs rose 3.7 pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Italian refinery runs rose 3.7 pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian refinery runs rose 3.7 percent to 36.5 million tonnes in the first five months of 1997, according to trade body Unione Petrolifera (UP).</p>
<p>It said crude refinery runs rose 0.7 percent over this period while imported semi-finished products rose 43.1 percent.</p>
<p>UP said the cost of imported crude, equal to 244,100 lire per tonne, posted an increase of 9.5 percent due to 4.2 percent higher prices quoted in U.S. dollars and a 5.2 percent appreciation of the U.S. currency against the lira.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
